My first archeologist ascension.  I'd been trying to do one for a while but
couldn't get too far for lack of a good weapon and just being impatient.  So
this time I had two strategies: 1. Do the early protection racket (never
done it before, I considered it cheap), and 2. Go for Grayswandir.  Why else
be a lawful archeologist?

Plan 1 worked great.  I got down to minetown with my large dog Roo and a
couple cats I'd recruited.  Got to +1 base AC with my sold gems and money
vault loot at XP1.  Having good AC early in the game helps tremendously.

Later in the mines I came across a doozy of a bones level (thanks Hearse)
which I detailed here:
http://groups.google.com/groups?selm=meidnZUD96IembDdRVn-uA%40comcast.com
where my dog Roo became a purple worm and saved me from a Jabberwock, master
mind flayer and other assorted bad guys.

I kept Roo until he poly'd into something useless at around level 15, so I
went on without him.

Plan 2, for Grayswandir didn't work out very well since 4 or 5 artifacts had
already been created.  At the castle I decided to wish for it no matter how
many times it slipped away.  Well it slipped away every time so I wasted all
those wishes.  I decided to quit at this point, but then resolved to press
on anyway.  I had only Snickersnee +1 and Sunsword +5, finding very few
scrolls of enchant weapon.  My armor was all throw-away except my Hawaiian
shirt.

The rest of the game was unremarkable except that the random stuff generator
was really really stingy.  I never saw a lot of things: Magic Marker, ring
of regeneration, or bag of holding - 3 staples.  I poly'd for a bag and
wished for magic markers.  Eventually I cleared out all but Rodney's castle
so I went there in search of some useful scrolls - anything useful really.
There I found another wand of wishing!  I fixed my AC down to about -30 and
got speed, brilliance and fireproofed all my stuff.  This was in effort to
increase my spellcasting since I thought with only Sunsword and Snickersnee
I'd need it.  Finally right before Rodney I found a silver saber (been
looking for one all game long), got it to +7 and my other two main weapons
increased to +6 or +7 as well, and I was off two-weaponing.  I switched
between the two longswords as required, depending on where I was.

On my way back up I went back to my loot pile and discovered the stash I'd
made from the bones levels but forgot about!  Multitudes of cursed potions
and scrolls became holy water and blank scrolls.

At one point I found my faithful Roo had been turned into a baby green
dragon, so I decided to try to ascend with him.  I have never escaped with
my original pet so I went for it.  I raised him to adulthood, but alas he
died quickly in the first elemental plane and I had no way to revive him.
(my spell of extra healing had been forgotten, and I lost the book
somewhere).

Remarkable moments:
* Towards the end: You fall into the pit.  Spikes are poisoned!  You die!
But wait!  Your medallion glows...  - I had lost poison resistance
somewhere.  The esc key strikes again.

* Completely amnesia'd 3 times by mind flayers, causing me to lose good
armor twice by drinking unidentified potions of polymorph.  I was careless
this game, I'm lucky to have made it.

* I became a female at another point, but little changed in my stats.

* No Ludios this time.

* You can never have too many wands of digging.  Must have used 30 of them.

* For the first time I resorted to using a nymph to remove a cursed item
(lev boots).  Again I was just careless.

* Next time I will try to be a Xorn and eat some useful rings.  The
ring-swap dance would be nice to forget about.

* During my escape with the amulet I began to wonder if it was
mathematically possible to get out - I kept getting zapped downward 3 levels
for every 2 I went up, ending up at rock-bottom at least 5 times.

* In the endgame I went from ~290 ~190 HPs while facing Death, Pestilence
and Famine *all at once.*   During some point in the fracas my other "oLS
saved me, but again the esc key caused me to miss it, my 3rd amulet left
idle in my bag.

* At the second altar I lost my Snickersnee and Saber, leaving me with only
Sunsword to finish.  I'm glad I kept a backup weapon - didn't have to use
Sting, which was my main weapon for the 1st half.  Where did they go??

The 3rd altar was my own - in the other two I wiped out all the priests, but
I sprinted for the 3rd one and got outta there post-haste.


